                  }
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#5dChernSimonsTerm 5d Chern-Simons term
          %p
            The theory has a 2-form
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+density"} flux density
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_2
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mi d
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_2 = d A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/5d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 5d Chern-Simons theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            locally of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∝
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \propto \int_X F_2 \wedge F_2 \wedge A
            (
            %a{:href => "#Cremmer81"}> Cremmer 1981, p. 276
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#ChamseddineNicolai80"} Chamseddine &amp; Nicolai 1980 (4)
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#CastellaniDAuriaFre"} Castellani-D’Auria-Fre (III.5.70)
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GauntlettMyersTownsend98"} Gauntlet, Myers &amp; Townsend 1998, p. 3
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GGHPR02"} GGHPR 02 (2.1)
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BonettiGrimmHohenegger13"} Bonetti-Grimm-Hohenegger 13
          %p
            Hence the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+field"} bosonic field
            sector of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo =
                  %mn 5
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=5
            supergravity is
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein-Maxwell+theory"} Einstein
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxwell-Chern-Simons+theory"} Maxwell
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D5+Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            in 5D, where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equation+of+motion"} equation of motion
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+density"} flux density
            is of the non-linear form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mn 3
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mn 2
                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathrm{d} F_3
                  \\;=\;
                  F_2 \wedge F_2
                  \\mathrlap{\,,}
          %p
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo ⋆
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_3 \coloneqq \star F_2
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+dual"} Hodge dual
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_2
            (cf.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#GGHPR02"} GGHPR 02 (2.2)
          %p
            This is reflected in the corresponding cochains on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 5
                      %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi A
                  %mphantom
                    %mi AAA
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mrow
                      %mi string
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 5
                      %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi A
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mu_{D0,5d} = \overline{\psi}_A \psi_A
                  \\phantom{AAA}
                  \\mu_{string,5d} = \overline{\psi}_A\Gamma_a \psi_A  \wedge e^a
          %p satisfying
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mrow
                      %mi string
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 5
                      %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 5
                      %mi d
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 5
                      %mi d
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d \mu_{string,5d} = \mu_{D0,5d} \wedge \mu_{D0,5d}
                  \\,.
          %p
            due to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fierz+identity"} Fierz identity
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#CastellaniDAuriaFre"} Castellani-D’Auria-Fré 91 (III.5.50a)
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "Fierz+identity#QuadraticFierzIdentitiesIn5d"} this example
          %p
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/FierzIdentitiesForBraneCocyclesIn5d.png", :width => "600px"}/
          %p
            (the other Fierz identity (III.5.50a) gives the cocycle for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/membrane"} membrane
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+2-brane+in+5d"}> super 2-brane in 5d
            )
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mrow
                        %mi membrane
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 5
                        %mi d
                    %mo ≔
                    %mfrac
                      %mi i
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo ¯
                      %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mi b
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi a
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_{membrane,5d} \coloneqq \frac{i}{2}\overline{\psi}_A \Gamma_{a b}  \psi \wedge e^a \wedge e^b
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mrow
                        %mi membrane
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 5
                        %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \mu_{membrane,5d} = 0
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
          %p
            This is a lower dimensional analogue to the situation for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field"} C-field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_4
            (locally
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 4
                    %mo =
                    %mi d
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_4 = d C
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∝
                  %mo ∫
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \propto \int G_4 \wedge G_4 \wedge C
            and hence the equation of motion
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 7
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo −
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d G_7
                  \\;=\;
                  \-\tfrac{1}{2}G_4 \wedge G_4
          %p
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 7
                    %mo =
                    %mo ⋆
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_7 = \star G_4
          %h3#black_holes_and_black_strings Black holes and black (st)rings
          %p
            The first
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+ring"} black ring
            solution in 5d sugra was found in (
            %a{:href => "#ElvangEmparanMateosReall04"}> Elvang-Emparan-Mateos-Reall 04
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#ElvangEmparanMateosReall05"} Elvang-Emparan-Mateos-Reall 05
          %p
            Supersymmetric black holes exist precisely only in dimensions 4 and 5 (
            %a{:href => "#GauntlettMyersTownsend98"}> Gauntlett-Myers-Townsend 98
            ). These play a key role in the discussion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+holes+in+string+theory"} black holes in string theory
          %p
            (There are supersymmetric particle-like solutions of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 5
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \gt 5
            supergravity theories that are sometimes called black holes, but these are always singular. There are also supersymmetric black holes in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-de+Sitter+spacetime"} anti-de Sitter spacetime
            rather than asymptotically flat. Of course, there are non-singular supersymmetric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black brane
            solutions in various
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \geq 4
            supergravity theories but these are neither ‘particle-like’ nor, strictly speaking, asymptotically flat.)
          %h3#ViaCYCompactificationOf11dSupergravity Relation to 11D supergravity
          %div
            %p
              %strong
                Structural similarity between
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D11+supergravity"} D=11
                and minimal
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D5+supergravity"} D=5 supergravity
              %br/
              (cf.
              = succeed ";" do
                %a{:href => "5D+supergravity#MizoguchiOhta98"} Mizoguchi &amp; Ohta 1998
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "5D+supergravity#FujiiKemmokuMizoguchi99"} Fujii, Kemmoku &amp; Mizoguchi 1999
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "5D+supergravity#FujiiKemmokuMizoguchi00"} 2000
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk+spacetime"} bulk spacetime
